<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">European colonization of the Americas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century–19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European colonization of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> took place mainly between the late 15th century and the early 19th century, after the voyages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>; the Norse had earlier settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> and, around 1000, briefly a site near the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, Portugal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> claimed land and resources, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tordesillas">Treaty of Tordesillas</a> of 1494 divided the world between Portugal and Spain. Colonization brought the displacement, enslavement and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of the Indigenous peoples of the Americas and the founding of settler colonial states.</p></div>
